# Agent Rules

## Architecture Contract
Every agent in this system follows the orchestrator-worker pattern from `design.md`.
Read the Agent Map section of `design.md` before writing any agent code.

## Never Do These
- NEVER mix agent roles in one file or one function
- NEVER return full JSON from an agent to the orchestrator — return `analysis_id` only
- NEVER read from another agent's output directly — always read from PostgreSQL via `analysis_id`
- NEVER let one agent failure crash the entire pipeline — use `return_exceptions=True`
- NEVER skip writing to the `agent_runs` table — every agent run must be logged

## Always Do These
- One agent = one file = one responsibility
- Every agent reads input from PostgreSQL via `analysis_id`
- Every agent writes output directly to PostgreSQL before returning
- Every agent logs start/end timestamps and token count to `agent_runs`
- Wrap every external API call in `try/except`

## Null Output Contract
- Agent writes `{}` or null fields → legitimate empty result → continue, flag the gap
- Agent writes NOTHING to DB (silent crash) → retry once → halt with clear error if still null
- NEVER continue pipeline with a null DB write — downstream agents will hallucinate

## Parallel Execution (Data Harvester)
- All active sources fetched via `asyncio.gather()` simultaneously
- `return_exceptions=True` — one source failure NEVER kills the rest
- Failed sources logged to `sources_failed` array in output JSON

## Complexity Tiers
- Simple: 3 sources, 3-5 tool calls each
- Standard: 5 sources, 5-10 tool calls each  
- Complex: all 7 sources, 10-15 tool calls each
- NEVER over-invest in simple queries

## Search Strategy (Data Harvester)
- Start with short broad queries (1-3 words)
- Evaluate results, then narrow progressively
- NEVER start with long specific queries
